Assertions:
[ERRORS label=balance_before] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=balance_before] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC} — the fixture funds this account above the cheapest PTS line, so a later refusal cannot be a shortfall
[ERRORS label=addpts_spend] errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT label=readcart_spend] data.cart.validationErrors[*?errorCode=LOYALTY_INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE].length = 0 {SPEC} — a buyer with no organization holds their points personally; a store setting about organizations must not make them unspendable
[ERRORS label=place_spend] errors[] empty {SPEC}
[DATA label=place_spend] data.createOrderFromCart.number is non-null {SPEC}

[ERRORS label=read_path] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=read_path] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC} — on an Organization-mode store the read path must still resolve a personal balance for an actor who has no organization
[ERRORS label=history_path] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=history_path] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.totalCount > 0 {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=rest_user_log] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[DATA label=rest_user_log] body.results.length > 0 {SPEC} — the same actor's rows must be reachable user-scoped as well, so the storefront figure and the back-office figure describe one account

[ERRORS label=user_log] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=org_log] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[COUNT label=org_log] body.results.length > 0 {SPEC} — the control: the member's earn IS in the ledger at organization scope
[COUNT label=user_log] body.results.length > 0 {SPEC} — and the same row must stay reachable by the member's own UserId, which is what the contact blade and every support query read
[ERRORS label=user_bal] HTTP 200 {DOC}

[ERRORS label=org_bal] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=org_log] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[COUNT label=org_log] body.results.length > 0 {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=gql_bal] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=gql_bal] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{ORG_BAL}} {SPEC} — the pooled figure the back office reports and the pooled figure a member reads are one number, or nobody can reconcile what the company holds
[DATA label=sib_bal] body.balance < {{ORG_BAL}} {SPEC} — the outlet's earns stayed in the outlet and did not leak into the sibling organization

[ERRORS label=set_customer] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=set_org] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=bal_customer] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=bal_org] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_org] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{BAL_CUSTOMER}} {SPEC} — turning company points ON must not make a buyer's accumulated points unreachable; the story adds an organization-level total, it does not declare existing balances forfeit
[DATA label=progress_org] data.loyaltyMissionProgress.totalCount ≈ {{PROGRESS_COUNT_CUSTOMER}} {SPEC} — nor may it restart mission progress, which would permit a second reward for an already-completed mission

[ERRORS label=set_customer] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=restore_org] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=bal_customer] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_customer] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC} — points the member really earned during the organization window must still be worth something to somebody after the merchant changes their mind; a zero means they are reachable from neither scope
[ERRORS label=org_bal_after] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[DATA label=org_bal_after] body.balance ≈ {{ORG_BAL_BEFORE}} {SPEC} — the mode switch is a setting write with no data migration, so rows must keep the scope key they were written with rather than silently moving

[ERRORS label=place_a1] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=place_b1] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=log_after] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[DATA label=log_after] body.results.length ≈ {{ROWS_BEFORE}} + 2 {SPEC} — two orders settling together produce two ledger rows in the organization's pool; a lost update drops one silently and the company is credited for one purchase instead of two
[COUNT label=log_after] body.results.length > 0 {DOC}

[ERRORS label=locked_bal] errors[] non-empty {HYPOTHESIS} — losing organization membership should lose access to organization money; verify whether the pooled balance is refused or served
[ERRORS label=locked_history] errors[] non-empty {HYPOTHESIS} — verify whether the pooled LEDGER is refused as well, or only the balance
[EVIDENCE] record verbatim what the locked member could still read: the pooled balance figure, the pooled ledger totalCount, and whether any returned row belongs to a colleague {HYPOTHESIS}

[ERRORS label=caller_org] errors[] non-empty {SPEC} — a caller must not be able to name which organization's points to read
[ERRORS label=own_scope] errors[] empty {DOC} — the control: the same member's ambient-scope read succeeds, so the refusal above is about the argument and not about the account
[DATA label=own_scope] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance >= 0 {DOC}

[ERRORS label=other_user] errors[] non-empty {SPEC} — the guard must REFUSE; an empty successful response is not acceptable evidence because it reads as clean
[NULL label=other_user] data.loyaltyPointsHistory is null {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=own_user] errors[] empty {DOC} — the control: the same caller's own read succeeds, so the refusal above is about the userId and not about the session

[ERRORS label=bal_no_store] errors[] non-empty {SPEC} — storeId is String! on this build, so the query must be rejected rather than silently answered from an assumed store
[ERRORS label=hist_no_store] errors[] non-empty {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=bal_with_store] errors[] empty {DOC} — the control: the same query WITH storeId succeeds, so the two refusals above are about the missing argument
[DATA label=bal_with_store] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance >= 0 {DOC}

[ERRORS label=set_customer] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=restore_org] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=bal_noorg] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_noorg] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=hist_noorg] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=hist_noorg] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.totalCount > 0 {SPEC}
[ERRORS label=bal_member] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_member] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance < {{NOORG_BAL}} {SPEC} — in Customer mode the two accounts read their OWN figures, so an organization member does not inherit the personal shopper's balance
[ERRORS label=progress_member] errors[] empty {DOC}

[ERRORS label=contact] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=tf_bal] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=br_bal] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=multi_bal] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=contact] body.defaultOrganizationId is non-null {SPEC} — the contact must declare a default organization, or the question this case asks is not decidable and the result is BLOCKED rather than a pass
[DATA label=multi_bal] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{TF_BAL}} {SPEC} — a contact who belongs to two companies must have their points resolved against the organization they actually default to, not whichever one an unordered collection happens to list first

[ERRORS label=place_a1] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=place_a2] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=place_b1] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_b0] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{BAL_A2}} {SPEC} — before B orders at all, B already reads A's pooled total: the pool belongs to the organization, so the bonus question is about the organization and not about B
[DATA label=bal_a1] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{BAL_A0}} + {{BAL_A2}} - {{BAL_A1}} {SPEC} — A's first and second identical orders are worth the same, which establishes the per-order rate free of any first-order bonus
[DATA label=bal_b1] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{BAL_B0}} + {{BAL_A2}} - {{BAL_A1}} {SPEC} — B's FIRST order in an organization that has already ordered is worth exactly that same per-order rate; a larger delta is a new-customer bonus firing a second time for one company

[BLADE] the organization details blade for '@td(ORG_LOY_A.org_name)' renders a loyalty widget in its widget strip {SPEC}
[DOM] WIDGET_BALANCE is present and equals the balance GET /api/loyalty-program-operation-log/balance/organization/@td(ORG_LOY_A.org_id) returns for the same organization at the same moment {SPEC}
[DOM] WIDGET_BALANCE is present and greater than 0 {SPEC} — the fixture organization has earned, so a literal 0 here is a failed request rendered as a real figure
[GRID] WIDGET_ROWS is greater than 0 and every listed row belongs to this organization {SPEC}

[ERRORS label=place_mix] errors[] empty {DOC}
[ERRORS label=log_after] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[DATA label=log_after] body.results[*?operationType=Earned].length ≈ {{EARNED_BEFORE}} + 1 {BL} — exactly one Earned row per order, under the new organization scope as under the old user scope
[DATA label=log_after] body.results[*?operationType=Redeemed].length ≈ {{REDEEMED_BEFORE}} + 1 {BL} — and exactly one Redeemed row; a company credited or debited twice for one purchase is what this guard exists to prevent

[ERRORS label=set_customer] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[ERRORS label=restore_org] HTTP 200 {DOC}
[DATA label=bal_org] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC} — the case is vacuous against an empty pool; a zero here is BLOCKED, not a pass
[DATA label=bal_immediately_after] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance < {{BAL_ORG}} {SPEC} — the very next read after the write already resolves the new scope, with no cached-setting lag a merchant would have to wait out
[DATA label=bal_restored] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance ≈ {{BAL_ORG}} {SPEC} — and restoring the setting restores the scope just as immediately

[ERRORS label=pool_control] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA label=pool_control] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 {SPEC} — an unlocked colleague reads the pool immediately before the locked read; a zero here makes the two readings agree trivially and the case must report BLOCKED rather than pass
[COUNT label=history_control] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.totalCount > 0 {SPEC} — the same decidability gate on the ledger
[DATA label=locked_bal] data.loyaltyBalance.currentBalance > 0 OR errors[] non-empty {HYPOTHESIS} — a revoked member must be told they are refused; a served 200 carrying zero against a funded pool is exactly what a company that has never earned returns, so nothing on the response lets the customer tell revocation from an empty account
[DATA label=locked_history] data.loyaltyPointsHistory.totalCount > 0 OR errors[] non-empty {HYPOTHESIS} — the same distinguishability requirement on the pooled ledger
[EVIDENCE] record the locked member's balance figure and ledger totalCount beside the unlocked colleague's, both read in the same minute, and record whether any returned row belongs to a colleague {HYPOTHESIS}
